  "scope": "Finite ordinary existential growth in a fixed presentation, a nonempty allowed set, and freely chosen, total local readings on one common nonnegative weighting. The embodied-register theorem requires a uniform finite affine source, affine selectors with all four cells present, and affine marked registers.",
  "claim": "Finite ordinary parity and not-all-equal growth preserve old allowed states by projection. Every fixed weighting and setting-independent pair of external reads admits a common explanation, giving all eight CHSH bounds and both no-signalling equalities. For uniform affine states with affine embodied selectors, hiding the other selector in each full affine register is equivalent to a common local-source representation of all full-register tables, including nonlinear local postprocessing.",
  "argued_in_prose": [
    "Surjectivity of restriction through all finite funded rounds, and exact extension multiplicities.",
    "Common weighted pushforward on every prospective answer, exact CHSH and no-signalling for arbitrary local read functions, and individual-event extension for exact supports.",
    "Equivalence of full-register remote-selector invariance and existence of a common local model for uniform affine registers, plus the singleton-pattern answer-only corollary.",
    "One changed context attains the sharp score change 2t on altered mass t. Three perfect correlators preclude a quantum realization of this family whenever t is positive.",
    "A separate joint weighting of two disjoint parity knots matches an explicit quantum table at w=5:1. Above the quantum correlator ceiling it gives superquantum tables. These weightings are supplied."
  ],
